# Graphite stack PRs

For stacked or multi-PR work in this repo, use **Graphite only**.

## Do

- Create stack branches with `gt create` (child branch while checked out on its parent).
- Submit with `gt submit` or `gt submit --stack`.
- Use `gh` for read-only ops (`gh pr view`, `gh issue view`, `gh pr checks`) when useful.

## Do not

- Do **not** open stacked PRs with `gh pr create`, `gh pr create --fill`, or the GitHub UI “compare & pull request” flow for a stack.
- Do **not** push a child branch and independently `gh pr create` against `main` when it should stack on another feature branch.

## Examples

```bash
# Good — real Graphite stack
gt create feat/ts-sidecar -m "Migrate sidecar to TypeScript"
# ... implement, commit ...
gt create feat/pm2-manager -m "Add PM2 manager and logrotate"
# ... implement, commit ...
gt submit --stack

# Bad — breaks the stack
gh pr create --title "..." --body "..."
```

After submit, confirm in Graphite that the upper PR targets the lower branch (not both → `main` unless that is intentional for a single PR).
